    LLM: 'Game: Three Card Poker. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Three Card Poker is a popular casino table game based on poker. Players compete against the dealer. It features two modes of play: Ante/Play (playing against the dealer) and Pair Plus (betting on the hand value alone). It is known for its speed and simplicity.',
    objective: "Beat the dealer's hand with a higher 3-card poker hand.",
    gameplay: '1. Ante bet (and optional Pair Plus). 2. Deal 3 cards. 3. Player decides to Play (match Ante) or Fold (lose Ante). 4. Dealer reveals hand. Dealer must qualify with Queen High or better. 5. Compare hands. Scoring: Straight Flush > Three of a Kind > Straight > Flush > Pair > High Card. (Note: Straight beats Flush in 3-card poker, usually).',
